Description: docs/system/arm: Document the Chumby Classic machine
 The emulated devices and what is missing, how to boot the stock
 firmware, the board's lines, identity, sensor card, audio and USB
 (the stock root disk mounts a stick's first partition on /mnt/usb),
 the watchdog, and a command line for interactive use.
 .
 That is without -icount: -icount shift=auto,sleep=off boots fast but
 is wrong for a person at the screen. Measured with the stock firmware
 on an otherwise busy host, without -icount /proc/uptime advanced
 61.13 s over 61.13 s of host time, while with -icount
 shift=auto,sleep=off it advanced 153 s over 21 s with the guest idle,
 and QEMU used a whole host core instead of 10% of one; a tap sent with
 input-send-event reached a guest process reading /dev/input/event0 72
 to 83 ms later.
 .
 A "Frontend interface" section lists what frontends rely on: the
 machine properties, the state query, the events, the input conventions
 and screendump, which will not change incompatibly without a note
 there.
